# Suites expected to fail on this branch
# ======================================
#
# This branch adds the host test suites WITHOUT the source fixes they assert.
# That is deliberate: the tests are a detector, and the team decides whether to
# take the fixes or to schedule the work. Every entry below is a defect the
# suite has found in code this branch does not touch.
#
# run-tests reads this file and reports these separately from real regressions:
#
#   - a suite listed here that fails  -> "failed as expected", the run still
#                                        exits 0
#   - a suite listed here that PASSES -> reported loudly and the run FAILS, the
#                                        same polarity as the harness's XPASS.
#                                        The fix has landed; delete the line.
#   - anything else that fails        -> an unexpected failure, exit 1
#
# So the file has to be maintained: it is not a way to silence a test, it is a
# statement that a specific defect is still present. Deleting a line is how a
# fix gets acknowledged.
#
# Format, whitespace separated:
#
#   <suite>  <fix>  <what the suite detects>
#
# <fix> is the commit on Features/unit-test that makes the suite pass, for
# whoever picks the work up. Full details for every entry are in DEFECTS.md.

